WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.133
-Thank you very much,
and welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.467
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:05.467
You're here.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:10.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.334
Well, guys,
after a crazy four days,

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:15.834
March Madness is down
to the Sweet 16.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.834
That's right.
We are down to 16 teams.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.334
Three number-one seeds

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.767
and nine million commercials
for AT&amp;T.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.267
Yeah.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.534
Of course, the Cinderella story
that everyone's talking about

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:28.901
is the 15th-seed
Saint Peter's Peacocks

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:30.634
who have made it
to the Sweet 16.

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:32.267
It's exciting for long-time fans

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:35.033
who have been following the team
since Thursday.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.901
[ Laughter ]
And, uh...

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.934
Saint Peter's is the first team
from New Jersey

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:44.801
to make the Sweet 16
in over 20 years.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:49.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.567
And if they go all the way,
they'll be the only team

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.968
to wear their championship rings
on their pinkies.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:57.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.634
N-C-A-Ohh!

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.968
Hey! Ohh! This guy!

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.601
How can you not love their name?
They're the Peacocks.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.567
This is the best thing
that happened to NBC

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.067
since the new "Law &amp; Order."

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.067
[ Laughter ]
I love it.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.267
Let's get to some news.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.067
Well, guys, today
confirmation hearings began

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:18.667
for Supreme Court nominee
Ketanji Brown Jackson.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:21.434
The hearing process
will last four days.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.734
It's basically C-SPAN's version
of Coachella.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.334
And I saw that the top
Republican leading the hearings,

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:30.467
Chuck Grassley, is 88 years old.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:32.200
Wow.
When it was his turn to speak,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.701
he was like,
"Tell us who you are

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.334
and then tell me who I am."

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.567
Yep, Jackson will face days
of tough questions.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.000
Brett Kavanaugh was like...

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.701
[Slurring] "It'll be fine.
I did it for four days.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:47.767
After the s-second day...

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.534
After the --
After the second day,

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:50.968
it's kind of a blur. It's fine.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.167
It's like --

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:55.534
You're my best friend.
Hold my hair."

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:57.434
[ Imitates vomiting ]

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:59.033
But this is cool.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.033
I saw that
Judge Jackson's parents

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.767
were at
the confirmation hearing.

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.701
Even crazier,
so were Chuck Grassley's.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.067
[ Laughter ]
-Really?!

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.100
-Hey, you guys
remember last year

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.934
when that huge ship
blocked up the Suez Canal?

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:17.734
Well, the same company that owns
that ship is back in the news,

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.868
and it's for exactly
the reason that you think.

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.167
Listen to this.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.701
-A massive cargo ship
is stuck in the mud

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.334
off the coast of Maryland.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.501
The vessel,
called the "Ever Forward,"

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:30.400
grounded in the Chesapeake Bay.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.167
-Yeah, the "Ever Forward"
got stuck.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.934
Which is why they're
renaming it the "Irony."

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.567
Every few months, the owner gets
a call from the captain like,

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.834
"Okay. Don't be mad..."

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.467
Alright, listen to this.
I heard that Match just launched

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.968
a new dating app
for single parents called Stir.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.767
[ Audience ohhs ]
Yep.

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:59.400
Their slogan is, "I'll join
your hell if you join mine."

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.701
[ Applause ]

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:09.634
And this is fun.
Today after a two-year hiatus,

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:12.534
Dairy Queen's
Free Cone Day returned!

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:13.701
-Wow!

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.534
-And after
their two-year hiatus,

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.501
the McDonald's ice-cream machine
is still on hiatus.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.734
I'm sorry.

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:26.334
Finally, guys, in Miami, a thief
broke into a sneaker store

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.968
and took 20 shoes.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:32.133
But when he got out, he realized
he only stole the left sneakers.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:35.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.934
Officers were like --
[Imitates radio static]

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.434
"The suspect is 5'10",
200 pounds,

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:41.000
and running in circles."

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.400
No matter what happens,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.300
I hope he realizes that 20 lefts
do not make a right.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.100
Today in Washington,

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.868
it was Day 2
of confirmation hearings

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:53.934
for Supreme Court nominee
Ketanji Brown Jackson.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:56.000
-Whoo!
-Yep, these hearings are never

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.567
really fun, but then again,

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.000
there's always a paper crinkle

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.968
to really liven things up.
Watch this.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.300
Uh, unfortunately,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.834
[ Page turns ]
there's a 77% record --

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:09.133
I'm sorry.
Let me make sure

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.400
[ Laughter ]
that this is accurate.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.400
[ Pages turning ]

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.400
[ Laughter continues ]

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.567
[ Pages turning ]

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.467
[ Rubbing microphone ]

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.133
United States v Platz.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.167
Trump-appointed

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.734
Judge Sarah Pitlyk --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.701
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my goodness. Yeah, yeah.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:32.300
Even old people unwrapping hard
candy at the movies were like,

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.334
"Let's go, buddy, come on!"

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:37.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:40.067
Chomping on gum.
I love it.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:43.067
Yeah, Judge Jackson spent
all day answering questions.

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:44.834
Meanwhile, can we see
the Republican senators

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.133
who are asking them?

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.234
Gosh, it looks like
the Employee of the Month wall

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:49.234
at Cracker Barrel.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:52.300
That's right,
today Judge Jackson spent hours

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.300
answering questions.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.300
Most Senators didn't get
to be there,

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.901
but here at "The Tonight Show,"
we got ahold

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.434
of the questions
they would've asked.

00:04:58.434 --> 00:04:59.767
-Really?
-Yeah, check these out.

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:03.067
First, we have...

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:04.067
They would've asked...

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.234
That's a question they had.
-Question.

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:12.767
-Up next we have...

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:13.767
He would've asked...

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.434
Finally, we have...

00:05:19.434 --> 00:05:20.434
He would've asked..

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.234
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That's a hard no on that one.

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.234
What?

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.567
Some more news --
President Biden just warned

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.667
that Russia could be
exploring options

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.734
for cyberattacks
against the U.S.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:37.033
Isn't that always true?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.734
It's kind of like saying
Michael Bublé is exploring

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:41.200
another Christmas album.
It's like, yeah,

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.501
pretty sure it's going
to happen.

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.667
Biden said that they could hit
power grids and water supplies.

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.000
And people were like, "Cool,
just let us know

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.534
when TikTok's in danger, okay?"

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:51.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:53.267
Meanwhile,
to protect yourself online,

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:54.667
experts are saying
that you should make

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:57.667
your passwords longer
than eight characters.

00:05:57.667 --> 00:05:59.234
[ Audience murmuring ]
Americans were like, "So,

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:02.167
12345678!"

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:05.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.701
Some business news --
Zoom has introduced

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.667
a new avatar feature
that lets users

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.601
show up to meetings
as an animal,

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:14.400
[ Laughter ]
like a dog, a rabbit, or a fox.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.767
Yeah. There's nothing
like getting laid off

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:18.334
by a fox in the Bahamas.

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:20.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:22.501
And, finally, a 101-year-old man

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:25.167
who dropped out of high school
in the 1930s

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:28.834
just got his diploma,
more than 80 years later.

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:32.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:34.334
Asked what he's going to do now,
the guy said,

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:35.801
"Spring break!"

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:36.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:38.200
Let's get to some news.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.367
Well, guys, today was
Judge Ketanji Brown Jackson's

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:44.200
final day facing questions
from senators

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.167
during her confirmation
hearings.

00:06:46.167 --> 00:06:49.200
That's right, after nearly
30 hours of questions.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.601
Whew, yeah.

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:53.033
Her husband was so scared to ask
what she wanted for dinner,

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:54.567
he just ordered
takeout from everywhere.

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.234
He's just like,
"Yeah, never mind, never mind.

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:58.033
Do you wanna watch Netflix --
no Netflix, okay.

00:06:58.033 --> 00:06:59.701
We'll just put a --
let's buy another TV.

00:06:59.701 --> 00:07:01.067
We'll put on
two things at once."

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:02.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.334
But this is great --
according to a new poll,

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:07.167
Judge Jackson already has
a record approval rating

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:10.234
among Americans
for a Supreme Court nominee.

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:11.534
Wow.

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:16.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:18.367
Right now, Biden's like,
"Hey, I nominated you.

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:20.100
It's only fair we split
that approval rating.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.501
Come on."

00:07:21.501 --> 00:07:22.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.734 --> 00:07:24.067
Yep, the only way
it could have been higher

00:07:24.067 --> 00:07:26.133
is if she ended today
with a water bottle flip.

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:29.234
It's like, "Oh, yeah!"

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:31.734
In other news, despite the
current state of affairs,

00:07:31.734 --> 00:07:35.667
Vladimir Putin is still planning
to attend the G20 summit

00:07:35.667 --> 00:07:38.267
with other world leaders
in Bali this fall.

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:40.367
[ Audience oohs ]

00:07:40.367 --> 00:07:41.701
Which explains
this year's theme...

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:43.334
"awkward."

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:44.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.501 --> 00:07:45.667
Seriously, what is he doing?

00:07:45.667 --> 00:07:46.901
It's like getting
kicked out of high school

00:07:46.901 --> 00:07:48.234
and then showing up
for the reunion.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:50.934
Like, "What's up, guys?"

00:07:50.934 --> 00:07:52.901
"No, you were -- No."

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:55.033
Yeah, it'll backfire on Putin
when he realizes

00:07:55.033 --> 00:07:57.133
it's not a G20 summit,
it's an intervention.

00:07:57.133 --> 00:08:02.767
He's like, "Wait a minute, I --
I remember you."

00:08:02.767 --> 00:08:05.133
Some business news,
apparently Apple has experienced

00:08:05.133 --> 00:08:08.734
two major outages
in the past two days.

00:08:08.734 --> 00:08:11.000
Luckily, the problem was fixed
when the guy at the Genius Bar

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.200
told Tim Cook to just drop the
entire company in a bag of rice.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:19.467
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.467 --> 00:08:21.000
Yeah, in the most recent outage,

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.234
Apple Music and Apple Books
went down,

00:08:24.234 --> 00:08:25.868
which means no one noticed.

00:08:25.868 --> 00:08:28.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.167
Apple Books?

00:08:30.167 --> 00:08:31.701
-Apple Books.

00:08:31.701 --> 00:08:33.601
-"Hey,
look it up on Apple Books."

00:08:35.367 --> 00:08:38.901
Hey, I saw that Taco Bell is
celebrating its 60th anniversary

00:08:38.901 --> 00:08:41.267
with an all-new vegetarian meal.

00:08:41.267 --> 00:08:43.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:43.501 --> 00:08:45.567
And actually, it's
the first time anyone's ever

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:47.767
said "Happy anniversary"
inside a Taco Bell.

00:08:47.767 --> 00:08:49.234
-Wow.

00:08:49.234 --> 00:08:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.701 --> 00:08:51.934
-Some TV news.

00:08:51.934 --> 00:08:54.534
CBS is releasing a new
dating competition show

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:57.667
called "The Real Love Boat,"
in which a big group of singles

00:08:57.667 --> 00:08:59.534
spend nearly a
month together on a cruise.

00:08:59.534 --> 00:09:00.634
-Ooh.

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:01.934
-Yep, it's the only dating show

00:09:01.934 --> 00:09:04.267
where the winner is
whoever gets kicked off first.

00:09:04.267 --> 00:09:06.467
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.467 --> 00:09:08.033
It's just like "The Bachelor,"

00:09:08.033 --> 00:09:10.300
but instead of a rose,
you get a bottle of imodium.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.334 --> 00:09:15.467
And finally, I saw that today
is National Puppy Day.

00:09:15.467 --> 00:09:20.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:21.167
Yep.

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:22.267
And not surprisingly,

00:09:22.267 --> 00:09:24.200
National Puppy Day
falls on Hump Day.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.834
[ Applause ]

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:28.534
Well, guys, earlier today
President Biden was in Brussels

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:32.934
to meet with NATO leaders for
an emergency summit on Russia.

00:09:32.934 --> 00:09:35.667
When they voted on a resolution
to condemn Putin,

00:09:35.667 --> 00:09:38.901
30 leaders voted "yea," and one
office plant voted "nyet."

00:09:38.901 --> 00:09:43.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.734
Anyone see that plant walk?
-Yeah.

00:09:45.734 --> 00:09:48.200
-Yeah, it was an emergency
summit, but don't worry.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.634
NATO leaders still had time
for a family photo.

00:09:50.634 --> 00:09:52.000
Here it is.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.200
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.067
Looks like the sales team at
a Honda dealership, doesn't it?

00:09:57.067 --> 00:09:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.901
I'm expecting them to all
say together,

00:10:00.901 --> 00:10:02.701
"We're ready to serve you."

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:04.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:04.667 --> 00:10:06.434
Can we see it again?

00:10:06.434 --> 00:10:07.834
Yeah.

00:10:07.834 --> 00:10:09.434
It's a very diverse group.

00:10:09.434 --> 00:10:11.033
There are suits of every color.

00:10:11.033 --> 00:10:12.601
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.601 --> 00:10:14.968
Yeah, that's either a NATO
summit or a conference for

00:10:14.968 --> 00:10:16.767
"men who don't know what to do
with their arms" photo.

00:10:16.767 --> 00:10:18.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.267 --> 00:10:26.968
Can we see the photo
just one more time?

00:10:26.968 --> 00:10:28.234
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.234 --> 00:10:33.801
♪♪

00:10:33.801 --> 00:10:36.033
There we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.033 --> 00:10:38.334
Kind of doing his own thing.
-Yeah.

00:10:38.334 --> 00:10:41.267
-Well, changing gears,
this morning the "Today" show

00:10:41.267 --> 00:10:43.601
investigated the dangers
of the metaverse.

00:10:43.601 --> 00:10:45.567
And they even sent
one of their reporters in

00:10:45.567 --> 00:10:47.000
to see what kind of activity
goes on in there.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.267
Let's see how that went.

00:10:48.267 --> 00:10:50.701
-We wanted to see the
concerns for ourselves,

00:10:50.701 --> 00:10:53.634
so I put on a headset and
entered the metaverse.

00:10:53.634 --> 00:10:55.167
That blue robot is me.

00:10:55.167 --> 00:10:57.434
There we entered
a virtual strip club,

00:10:57.434 --> 00:10:59.667
created and uploaded
by another user.

00:10:59.667 --> 00:11:03.067
-I am a reporter, yes, trying to
understand the metaverse.

00:11:03.067 --> 00:11:05.501
-[ High-pitched voice ] Oh, you
should not have come in here.

00:11:05.501 --> 00:11:07.901
[ Laughter ]

00:11:07.901 --> 00:11:09.133
-Oh, boy.

00:11:09.133 --> 00:11:11.934
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.934 --> 00:11:13.567
-Amazing!

00:11:13.567 --> 00:11:16.300
Billions spent on technology
so a cartoon weasel

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.868
can kick you out of
a fake strip club.

00:11:17.868 --> 00:11:19.267
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.267 --> 00:11:20.901
[ High-pitched voice ] You
should not have come in here.

00:11:20.901 --> 00:11:22.367
Oh, no.

00:11:22.367 --> 00:11:24.634
Put your hands together
for Cinnamon, everybody.

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.567
[ Normal voice ] Some business
news -- due to a shortage of

00:11:27.567 --> 00:11:30.067
ingredients, General Mills
is struggling to supply

00:11:30.067 --> 00:11:32.434
grocery stores with
Totino's Pizza Rolls

00:11:32.434 --> 00:11:33.934
and Pillsbury Cookie Dough.

00:11:33.934 --> 00:11:35.100
[ Audience ohs ]
-Oh.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.801
-It's serious.
As soon as he heard, Biden

00:11:36.801 --> 00:11:38.667
called NATO back for
another emergency summit.

00:11:38.667 --> 00:11:40.701
[ Laughter ]

00:11:40.701 --> 00:11:43.033
Honestly, when I heard there was
a T.P. shortage,

00:11:43.033 --> 00:11:44.634
I wasn't thinking
Totino's Pizza.

00:11:44.634 --> 00:11:46.434
[ Laughter ]

00:11:46.434 --> 00:11:47.801
Right now General Mills is like,

00:11:47.801 --> 00:11:50.133
"Hey, but we still have plenty
of Fiber One bars.

00:11:50.133 --> 00:11:53.434
Hello? Anyone?

00:11:53.434 --> 00:11:56.968
Anyone want to gnaw on
a Fiber One bar?"

00:11:56.968 --> 00:12:03.200
[ Laughter ]

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.634
One vote said, "Nyet."
One office plant said, "Nyet."

00:12:07.634 --> 00:12:10.167
-It was a spy. It was a Russian
spy, is what you're saying.

00:12:10.167 --> 00:12:11.634
-What's that?
-It was a Russian spy

00:12:11.634 --> 00:12:13.133
in that plant.
-Oh, is that correct?

00:12:13.133 --> 00:12:15.000
-Yeah, that's what it was.
That's why it said, "Nyet."

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.334
-Oh, so you're saying it's
"30 world leaders said yes."

00:12:17.334 --> 00:12:19.167
And then one office plant
said --

00:12:19.167 --> 00:12:21.300
-"Nyet," which is "no"
in Russian.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.701
-Yeah, and it was --
But a plant --

00:12:22.701 --> 00:12:25.334
-So you're implying that it was
a spy in that plant.

00:12:25.334 --> 00:12:26.501
That's what makes it
so humorous.

00:12:26.501 --> 00:12:27.767
That's what I love about it.

00:12:27.767 --> 00:12:32.467
[ Laughter ]

00:12:32.467 --> 00:12:34.133
Topical.

00:12:34.133 --> 00:12:35.901
-Yep, it is.

00:12:35.901 --> 00:12:37.234
Hey, this is big though, guys.

00:12:37.234 --> 00:12:39.801
Yesterday CEOs of every major
U.S. airline called on

00:12:39.801 --> 00:12:42.234
President Biden to drop
the federal mask mandate.

00:12:42.234 --> 00:12:43.334
-Ooh.
-Yep.

00:12:43.334 --> 00:12:44.868
[ Applause ]

00:12:44.868 --> 00:12:47.334
-Each airline actually released
its own statement about it.

00:12:47.334 --> 00:12:48.834
Take a look.
American Airlines said...

00:12:51.601 --> 00:12:52.934
United said...

00:12:55.667 --> 00:12:56.701
Spirit Airlines said...

00:12:58.434 --> 00:13:07.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:07.367 --> 00:13:08.701
And Delta said...

00:13:11.601 --> 00:13:12.701
Then Spirit said...

00:13:16.534 --> 00:13:17.534
[ Laughter ]

00:13:17.534 --> 00:13:18.767
JetBlue said...

00:13:21.801 --> 00:13:22.934
And finally, Spirit said...

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:26.634 --> 00:13:30.467
Pretty out of the loop,
I don't know.

00:13:30.467 --> 00:13:33.067
Hey, get this, I saw that Uber
has reached a deal

00:13:33.067 --> 00:13:36.367
to list all New York City taxis
on its app.

00:13:36.367 --> 00:13:38.467
And this makes sense --
they hashed out the deal

00:13:38.467 --> 00:13:40.767
by screaming at each other
through open car windows.

00:13:40.767 --> 00:13:42.767
"You want to sign the deal?
You sign it!"

00:13:42.767 --> 00:13:45.167
You can't park there!
Sign the deal! You" --

00:13:45.167 --> 00:13:47.100
[ Laughter ]

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:50.033
Hey, here's some good news.
I read that as kids

00:13:50.033 --> 00:13:53.701
return to the classroom,
their test scores are going up.

00:13:53.701 --> 00:13:57.467
It's a really nice way of saying
we all failed at homeschooling.

00:13:57.467 --> 00:13:58.934
[ Laughter ]

00:13:58.934 --> 00:14:01.000
Yep, first graders are already
coming home like,

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.267
[English accent] "Mother,
father, your homeschooling

00:14:02.267 --> 00:14:03.667
efforts were rather deficient."

00:14:03.667 --> 00:14:06.000
[ Laughter ]

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.033
[ Normal voice ]
I heard a new report about

00:14:08.033 --> 00:14:10.634
where people like to eat food
in their house.

00:14:10.634 --> 00:14:13.234
And the results might surprise
you. Check it out.

00:14:13.234 --> 00:14:15.400
-According to a new survey
in the U.K.,

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.501
more than
one in five people say

00:14:17.501 --> 00:14:19.934
they snack in the bathroom.

00:14:19.934 --> 00:14:23.667
18% confessed they enjoy
their treats on the toilet.

00:14:23.667 --> 00:14:25.434
-No!
-What?!

00:14:25.434 --> 00:14:26.601
-You know what?

00:14:26.601 --> 00:14:28.133
Just take me back
to the metaverse.

00:14:28.133 --> 00:14:29.501
I think I like that.

00:14:29.501 --> 00:14:32.267
[ High-pitched voice ]
"Welcome back, Mr. Fallon.

00:14:32.267 --> 00:14:35.901
Here's 70 Jimmy bucks for you
to make it rain."

00:14:35.901 --> 00:14:38.133
[ Laughter ]

00:14:38.133 --> 00:14:40.133
[ Normal voice ] Finally,
researchers say that they're

00:14:40.133 --> 00:14:42.400
getting closer to producing
the first ever

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.834
birth control pill for men.
-Ooh.

00:14:44.834 --> 00:14:49.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:49.534 --> 00:14:55.767
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:14:55.767 --> 00:14:58.601
-That's better than the original
form of male birth control --

00:14:58.601 --> 00:15:00.067
dress socks with sandals.

00:15:00.067 --> 00:15:01.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:01.367 --> 00:15:05.334
Well, guys, this Sunday is
the 94th Academy Awards.

00:15:05.334 --> 00:15:06.334
Yeah.

00:15:06.334 --> 00:15:08.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.767
That's right, the Oscars are 94,

00:15:09.767 --> 00:15:12.701
and typical Hollywood, they're
all dating statues in their 20s.

00:15:12.701 --> 00:15:14.400
[ Laughter ]

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:15.501
I can't wait.

00:15:15.501 --> 00:15:17.400
The biggest stars
walking the red carpet,

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.834
being asked "Who are you
wearing? Who swabbed you?"

00:15:19.834 --> 00:15:20.834
You know.

00:15:20.834 --> 00:15:22.000
[ Laughter ]

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.567
Quick heads-up, if you hear
a piercing shriek

00:15:24.567 --> 00:15:25.868
halfway through the show,

00:15:25.868 --> 00:15:28.000
that's just me
when Questlove wins the Oscar.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:34.868 --> 00:15:36.767
Meanwhile, Quest, you're
going to enjoy this, all right?

00:15:36.767 --> 00:15:41.133
So, the Oscar gift bag this year
has a value of $140,000.

00:15:41.133 --> 00:15:42.234
[ Audience oohs ]

00:15:42.234 --> 00:15:43.734
$140,000.

00:15:43.734 --> 00:15:44.834
Can we see what's in the bag?

00:15:45.767 --> 00:15:47.534
Oh, it's gas. Oh, fantastic.

00:15:47.534 --> 00:15:48.501
[ Laughter ]

00:15:48.501 --> 00:15:49.534
It's a gallon of gas.

00:15:49.534 --> 00:15:51.467
-Wow.
-A gallon -- a whole gallon.

00:15:53.567 --> 00:15:56.133
The big nominees this year
are "The Power of the Dog,"

00:15:56.133 --> 00:15:59.567
"CODA," "Belfast," and a bunch
of others you started streaming

00:15:59.567 --> 00:16:00.934
and forgot to finish.

00:16:00.934 --> 00:16:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:16:02.234 --> 00:16:03.534
But this is new.

00:16:03.534 --> 00:16:05.334
I saw that this year,
there's a Fan Favorite Award

00:16:05.334 --> 00:16:07.968
that will be decided
by a vote on Twitter.

00:16:07.968 --> 00:16:10.200
That's why the Oscar will go
to a TikTok

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.801
of a guy falling
off a golf cart.

00:16:11.801 --> 00:16:13.767
[ Laughter ]

00:16:13.767 --> 00:16:15.167
Well, this year, the Oscars
are paying tribute

00:16:15.167 --> 00:16:17.934
to "The Godfather"
for its 50th anniversary.

00:16:17.934 --> 00:16:18.934
They'll be like -- Yeah.

00:16:18.934 --> 00:16:20.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:21.934 --> 00:16:23.267
Yep, they're like,
"We're here to honor

00:16:23.267 --> 00:16:24.701
all the great
'Godfather' movies --

00:16:24.701 --> 00:16:26.667
'The Godfather,'
'Godfather: Part II.'

00:16:28.033 --> 00:16:29.734
You know, those two movies."

00:16:29.734 --> 00:16:31.367
[ Laughter ]

00:16:31.367 --> 00:16:32.868
That's right,
the Oscars will also pay tribute

00:16:32.868 --> 00:16:34.400
to the James Bond franchise.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:37.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:37.067 --> 00:16:40.367
It makes sense because there are
just so many classic Bond films.

00:16:40.367 --> 00:16:41.734
I mean, here,
check out this promo

00:16:41.734 --> 00:16:43.367
that The Academy just released.

00:16:43.367 --> 00:16:46.033
-This year, The Academy
is excited to take a look back

00:16:46.033 --> 00:16:48.567
at every James Bond film,
including...

00:17:02.467 --> 00:17:04.868
[ Laughter ]

00:17:04.868 --> 00:17:07.234
-A lot of great classics.
-Wow. Classic.

00:17:07.234 --> 00:17:09.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:09.267 --> 00:17:11.000
-[ Chuckles ]
-Wow.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.634
-Speaking of movies,
everyone is talking about this.

00:17:13.634 --> 00:17:16.634
The director of "The Batman"
just released a deleted scene

00:17:16.634 --> 00:17:19.868
showing Robert Pattinson
facing off against The Joker.

00:17:19.868 --> 00:17:22.033
-Ooh.
-It's pretty shocking.

00:17:22.033 --> 00:17:24.067
I had no idea that you could
release a three-hour movie

00:17:24.067 --> 00:17:25.334
and still have deleted scenes.

00:17:25.334 --> 00:17:26.501
[ Laughter ]

00:17:26.501 --> 00:17:27.868
Impossible.

00:17:27.868 --> 00:17:29.133
But the scene
is really something.

00:17:29.133 --> 00:17:30.901
I mean, we haven't seen
a Batman face off

00:17:30.901 --> 00:17:32.734
against The Joker in months.

00:17:32.734 --> 00:17:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:17:37.434 --> 00:17:38.901
Some TV news.

00:17:38.901 --> 00:17:40.367
Today, the second season
of "Bridgerton"

00:17:40.367 --> 00:17:42.033
started streaming on Netflix.

00:17:42.033 --> 00:17:43.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:43.234 --> 00:17:44.467
Oh, yeah.

00:17:44.467 --> 00:17:46.234
Mother's Day came early
this year.

00:17:46.234 --> 00:17:48.067
Yeah, that's right.
-Oh, oi.

00:17:48.067 --> 00:17:50.834
-At least I -- Apparently,
a lot of the fans were upset

00:17:50.834 --> 00:17:53.501
'cause this season
has way fewer sex scenes.

00:17:53.501 --> 00:17:55.067
[ Audience ohs ]
-Oh.

00:17:55.067 --> 00:17:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:17:56.968 --> 00:17:58.033
-I know.

00:17:58.033 --> 00:17:59.734
"Bridgerton"
without the sex scenes,

00:17:59.734 --> 00:18:01.667
which explains this new
Netflix message I saw.

00:18:03.067 --> 00:18:04.400
-Wow.

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:07.200
[ Laughter ]
-Isn't that weird?

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:09.734
Got even weirder when Netflix
added more sex scenes

00:18:09.734 --> 00:18:10.901
to "Is It Cake?"

00:18:10.901 --> 00:18:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:18:12.234 --> 00:18:13.634
Well, this is nice.

00:18:13.634 --> 00:18:16.033
Today, President Biden was
in Poland visiting our troops

00:18:16.033 --> 00:18:17.868
and even stayed for some pizza.

00:18:17.868 --> 00:18:20.400
But I think the jalapeño slice
caught him by surprise.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.901
Watch -- Watch this.

00:18:28.601 --> 00:18:30.000
[ Laughter ]

00:18:33.734 --> 00:18:36.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:18:37.434 --> 00:18:39.701
-Oh.

00:18:39.701 --> 00:18:41.067
-You -- [ Laughs ]

00:18:41.067 --> 00:18:43.133
You know it must have been bad
when during a pandemic,

00:18:43.133 --> 00:18:44.601
Biden is like,
"Let me drink from your cup.

00:18:44.601 --> 00:18:45.667
Let me --

00:18:45.667 --> 00:18:47.100
I need something to --
Hand it over.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:49.167
Just -- Just spit it
in my mouth.

00:18:49.167 --> 00:18:50.634
Just go -- I really --
I don't --

00:18:50.634 --> 00:18:53.300
Hot, hot, hot."

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.667
Yeah, the spice
really got to him.

00:18:54.667 --> 00:18:55.801
And this is real.

00:18:55.801 --> 00:18:57.100
He was still feeling it
a little later.

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:58.667
This is a real video.
Check it out.

00:18:58.667 --> 00:18:59.801
[ Coughing ]

00:19:12.834 --> 00:19:14.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:19:16.434 --> 00:19:18.100
-I love that dude.

00:19:19.801 --> 00:19:21.567
I love how he says "pizza pie."

00:19:21.567 --> 00:19:24.534
I don't even think
Mario and Luigi say that.

00:19:24.534 --> 00:19:26.334
[ Laughter ]

00:19:26.334 --> 00:19:27.801
It was like,
"You know what gives me

00:19:27.801 --> 00:19:29.367
worse heartburn that pizza pie?

00:19:29.367 --> 00:19:30.701
Pas-- Pasketti."

00:19:30.701 --> 00:19:32.701
[ Laughter ]

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:36.501
Some business news.

00:19:36.501 --> 00:19:40.968
IHOP and Pepsi have teamed up to
create the new maple syrup cola.

00:19:40.968 --> 00:19:41.901
Here it is.

00:19:41.901 --> 00:19:43.033
Yeah.

00:19:43.033 --> 00:19:44.367
[ Audience ohs ]

00:19:44.367 --> 00:19:45.767
Yeah, I'm trying to be healthy,
so I'm going to wait

00:19:45.767 --> 00:19:47.968
'til they come out
with a diet maple syrup Pepsi.

00:19:47.968 --> 00:19:49.834
[ Laughter ]

00:19:49.834 --> 00:19:51.868
Yeah, it turns out
the executives at IHOP

00:19:51.868 --> 00:19:53.234
are just as drunk
as the customers.

00:19:53.234 --> 00:19:54.567
[ Laughter ]

00:19:54.567 --> 00:19:55.934
And finally, a new study

00:19:55.934 --> 00:19:58.567
found that drinking two
to three cups of coffee a day

00:19:58.567 --> 00:20:00.968
could add years to your life.

00:20:00.968 --> 00:20:02.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:20:05.901 --> 00:20:08.834
On the flip side, if you want
to take years off of your life,

00:20:08.834 --> 00:20:11.000
try the new maple syrup Pepsi
from IHOP.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:11.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

